<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
ExportOptions for `xcodebuild -exportArchive`.

REPLACE_WITH_TEAM_ID stays as committed: `scripts/ios/export-ipa.sh
--method <m>` writes a temporary copy with the requested method and this
machine's team (from the gitignored Config/Team.xcconfig that
`scripts/ios/setup-team.sh` writes). So no one's team id is committed, and
this file is never churned by a setup or a release.

Committed as the release path: method app-store-connect with MANUAL
signing. export-ipa.sh pins the "Just My Weather App Store" profile into
the temp copy; manual signing reads that profile from disk instead of
asking Apple's cloud-signing service, which an App Manager-role API key
may not drive ("Cloud signing permission error"). For development /
ad-hoc exports the temp copy is flipped to automatic. Keep the
signingStyle key: export-ipa.sh refuses to run if the flip can't land.

Method values (Xcode 15.3+ names):
- "app-store-connect" → upload to App Store Connect / TestFlight (default here)
- "development"       → install on devices registered in your team
- "ad-hoc"            → install on a specific device list, outside the App Store

Bitcode (uploadBitcode / compileBitcode) was deprecated in Xcode 14
and removed in Xcode 15+, so those keys are intentionally omitted —
they'd be no-ops with current toolchains and only invite confusion.
-->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>method</key>
    <string>app-store-connect</string>
    <key>teamID</key>
    <string>REPLACE_WITH_TEAM_ID</string>
    <key>signingStyle</key>
    <string>manual</string>
    <key>stripSwiftSymbols</key>
    <true/>
    <key>uploadSymbols</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
